{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and the endpoint accepted it as the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. The frontend pod runs on `kind-worker2`, but the only recommendation pod runs on `kind-worker`. With the Local policy, the frontend's connections to the recommendation Service had no local endpoint and timed out. Calls to `/api/recommendations` either hung until the proxy's 15-second timeout (504) or returned 500 from the frontend.\n\n**Fix:** I patched the Service to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`. I also restarted the `frontend` deployment to clear its stale gRPC channel.\n\n**Verification:** Through `frontend-proxy`, `/api/recommendations` returned 200 in about 15 ms. `/`, `/api/products`, and `/api/cart` also returned 200, and all pods are Running.\n\n**Not changed:** The `otel-collector` Service also uses `Local`, which is expected for its DaemonSet, so I left it as is."}}
